====================================================================================================
G. Lateral decay lengths and what an IR camera could see
====================================================================================================
bare lid as a convectively cooled fin, sqrt(k t / h), t 0.5-1.3 mm, h 8-15: 131 / 175 / 224 mm  (plan: ~200 mm; t=1 mm, h=10 gives 197 mm)
lid with the heatsink on, sqrt(k t R"_TIM2), R" 0.1-0.5 K cm2/W: 1.93 / 3.12 / 4.45 mm (plan: ~3.7 mm)
heatsink OFF, die+lid composite over the substrate, sqrt((kt_lid+kt_si) R"_down), R"_down 5-20 K cm2/W: 15 / 22.8 / 30.7 mm  -> die ~22-26 mm wide: near-isothermal at shire scale (3.7 mm)
  1 W concentrated (one shire), heatsink off: excess at r = 2 mm: 0.712 / 0.935 / 1.33 C
  1 W concentrated (one shire), heatsink off: excess at r = 10 mm: 0.262 / 0.381 / 0.533 C
  1 W concentrated (one shire), heatsink off: excess at r = 20 mm: 0.106 / 0.19 / 0.264 C
lid following the die through TIM1, sqrt(k t R"_TIM1): 1.37 / 2.39 / 3.44 mm
delidded die under an IR-window liquid cooler (h 5e3-2e4 W/m2K), sqrt(k_Si t / h): 1.95 / 2.79 / 4 mm
  lock-in diffusion length in Si at 1 Hz, sqrt(alpha/(pi f)): 4.75 / 5.05 / 5.32 mm
  lock-in diffusion length in Si at 5 Hz, sqrt(alpha/(pi f)): 2.13 / 2.26 / 2.38 mm
  lock-in diffusion length in Si at 10 Hz, sqrt(alpha/(pi f)): 1.5 / 1.6 / 1.68 mm
shire pitch 3.7 mm (facts-numbers.json:1356); the P3 camera is LWIR 8-14 um, 25 Hz (plan 2a); sapphire is opaque there, so an IR-window cooler for it needs Ge/ZnSe and a LWIR-transparent coolant (none common): an MWIR camera job
